# Supabase project URL (safe to expose to the browser)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase anon/public key (safe to expose to the browser — protected by Row
# Level Security). Used only to sign the admin dashboard in and out via
# Supabase Auth at /admin/login. Get this from Supabase → Project Settings →
# API → Project API keys → anon / public.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Supabase service role / secret key — server-only, bypasses Row Level Security.
# Never expose this to the client or commit it to git.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Winsalot Growth CRM email ---

# Resend API key used to send CRM emails (follow-up emails, agent invites,
# opportunity alerts). Server-only. Get this from https://resend.com/api-keys
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Growth CRM weekly marketing (GET /api/cron/crm-weekly-marketing, daily -
# see vercel.json and src/lib/crm-marketing-job.ts). Host detection
# enables this only on the winsalot-funding/Growth project.
# CRM_MARKETING_CRON_ENABLED is an optional override that can explicitly
# disable it for an emergency or enable it in a nonstandard environment -
# never set it true on the Lead Generation CRM project.
#
# This route requires the SAME CRON_SECRET var documented in full below
# ("Shared secret every Vercel cron job in this app must present...") -
# it is NOT a separate/optional secret for this route specifically. Set
# CRON_SECRET as a Vercel project env var on winsalot-funding's
# Production environment (Project Settings -> Environment Variables),
# then redeploy - Vercel then automatically sends it as
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` on every scheduled invocation of every
# cron job in vercel.json for this project. Without it, this route always
# returns 401 and due contacts are never processed, even though the
# schedule/registration in vercel.json is otherwise correct - this is the
# single most common cause of "Next Email passed but Last Email/Sent
# never updated."
CRM_MARKETING_CRON_ENABLED=
CRON_SECRET=

# Winsalot Corp.'s physical head-office address, shown in every weekly
# marketing email's compliance footer, used to be read from this var at
# send time (WINSALOT_MAILING_ADDRESS) - which is exactly how the
# retired "20 Leacrest Street" address ended up live in production
# emails for so long after the office actually moved, with nothing in
# this codebase ever showing it was wrong. It's no longer read from here
# at all: the current address (55 Rutherford Road South, Suite 3,
# Brampton, Ontario L6W 3J3, Canada) is now a fixed constant in
# src/lib/crm-marketing-email.ts - update that one place, and only that
# place, the next time Winsalot Corp. changes offices. This var is kept
# here, deliberately left unset, only as a landmine warning: setting it
# again does nothing.
WINSALOT_MAILING_ADDRESS=

# Mailbox that receives internal notification emails.
NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=info@winsalotcorp.com

# --- Centralized sender identities (src/lib/email-senders.ts) ---
# Every email this app's Growth-side products send (consultation
# booking, opportunity follow-ups/consultation invites, and invoices)
# picks its "From" identity from src/lib/email-senders.ts, not from any
# of these vars directly - each is only an *override* for its own
# category's hardcoded default, so leave all four unset to get the
# correct identities out of the box:
#   growth  -> Winsalot Corp <info@winsalotcorp.com>   (consultations,
#              bookings, confirmations, reminders, rescheduling,
#              cancellations, and lead-generation/both-services
#              opportunity emails - same already-verified, already-warmed
#              address the Lead Generation CRM sends from)
#   funding -> Winsalot Corp <info@winsalotcorp.com>   (business-
#              financing opportunity emails - same address as growth,
#              for the same reason)
#   billing -> Winsalot Corp <billing@winsalotcorp.com> (invoices,
#              payment reminders, payment receipts)
#   quotes  -> Winsalot Corp <quotes@winsalotcorp.com>   (reserved for
#              the retired commercial-cleaning-quote system - no live
#              send path uses this today, kept isolated so it can never
#              be reached by the three categories above)
# Every category is branded as the company only - no agent's name appears
# as the sender display name.
# Every address must be on a domain verified in Resend (see
# https://resend.com/domains) or the send will fail/land in spam.
# Format: "Winsalot Growth <growth@winsalotcorp.com>"
GROWTH_EMAIL_FROM=
FUNDING_EMAIL_FROM=
BILLING_EMAIL_FROM=
QUOTES_EMAIL_FROM=

# "Reply-To" address shared by every one of the categories above.
# Falls back to info@winsalotcorp.com if unset.
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=

# Absolute base URL of this site, used to build the redirect link in
# admin/agent invite/forgot-password emails (see src/lib/site-url.ts).
#
# Set this to EXACTLY https://growth.winsalotcorp.com on the winsalot-funding
# project's Production environment - growth.winsalotcorp.com is the sole
# canonical Growth CRM domain (see src/lib/hosts.ts). Do NOT set this to
# https://cleaning.winsalotcorp.com (the retired domain Vercel now
# redirects to growth.winsalotcorp.com) - getSiteUrl() (src/lib/site-url.ts)
# rejects that specific value outright if it's ever set here anyway, but
# don't rely on that: correct the value in Vercel and redeploy, since the
# fix does not take effect until a new deployment is built.
#
# IMPORTANT: set this ONLY on the Production environment in Vercel
# (Project Settings -> Environment Variables -> scope to Production).
# Leave it unset on Preview - agent invite/reset links need to redirect
# back to the *same* preview deployment that sent them, not to
# production, and leaving this unset on Preview lets that fall back to
# the current deployment's own Vercel URL automatically. If unset on the
# winsalot-funding project's Production environment specifically,
# getSiteUrl() falls back to the real https://growth.winsalotcorp.com
# directly rather than an ambiguous Vercel deployment URL (see that
# function for why); getAuthRedirectBaseUrl() still falls back to the
# Vercel deployment URL, then localhost, since an auth redirect must land
# back on the same deployment that issued the email.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Shared secret every Vercel cron job in this app must present as
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` - every route listed in vercel.json's
# `crons` array checks this same var:
#   - GET /api/cron/leadgen-appointment-reminders (the Lead Gen CRM's
#     automatic 24-hour appointment reminder job - see
#     lib/leadgen-appointment-reminders.ts), daily.
#   - GET /api/cron/crm-weekly-marketing (the Growth CRM's weekly
#     marketing sender - see src/lib/crm-marketing-job.ts and the
#     dedicated note above), daily.
#   - GET /api/cron/agent-monthly-reports, monthly.
# Set this as a Vercel project env var (Production) and Vercel
# automatically sends it on every Cron Job invocation for any endpoint
# actually scheduled in vercel.json. Without it, that endpoint always
# returns 401. This same repo/vercel.json is deployed to BOTH the Growth
# CRM (winsalot-funding) and Lead Gen CRM (winsalot-leadgen-crm) Vercel
# projects, and each project's cron invocations only ever carry that
# project's own env vars - so this var must be set as its own value on
# EACH project independently, not just one of them.
CRON_SECRET=

# Gates GET /api/cron/leadgen-appointment-reminders so it only ever does
# real work on the Lead Gen CRM project. Both winsalot-funding (Growth
# CRM) and winsalot-leadgen-crm deploy the same repo and share one
# vercel.json, so both projects register this cron's schedule - Vercel has
# no per-project override for that. Set this to exactly "true" as a
# Production env var on winsalot-leadgen-crm ONLY. Leave it unset (or any
# other value) on winsalot-funding - the route returns a 200 no-op there
# immediately, before touching Supabase, Resend, or CRON_SECRET, so the
# Growth CRM's copy of this cron never sends a reminder or writes a row.
LEADGEN_REMINDER_CRON_ENABLED=

# Bearer secret for GET/POST /api/cron/leadgen-business-appointment-reminders
# (the Lead Gen CRM's automatic BUSINESS-facing 24-hour + 1-hour
# appointment reminder job - reminds the CRM client, e.g. Brent's
# Essentials, about their own upcoming appointments; see
# lib/leadgen-business-appointment-reminders.ts). Deliberately a separate
# secret from CRON_SECRET above: this route is invoked by Supabase's
# pg_cron/pg_net (see supabase/migrations/0068_leadgen_business_appointment_reminders.sql),
# not by Vercel Cron, since Vercel Cron on this account's Hobby plan can
# only run once a day - far too coarse for a "1 hour before" reminder.
# Set the SAME value here (as a Vercel project env var, Production only,
# on winsalot-leadgen-crm) and in Supabase Vault as the
# 'leadgen_business_reminder_cron_secret' secret - see that migration's
# header comment for the exact one-time setup steps. Also gated by
# LEADGEN_REMINDER_CRON_ENABLED above, same as the existing reminder cron.
LEADGEN_BUSINESS_REMINDER_CRON_SECRET=

# --- CRM email delivery tracking (Resend webhooks) ---
# See docs/crm.md#email-delivery-tracking for the full setup guide.

# Signing secret for the Resend webhook endpoint (POST /api/webhooks/resend).
# Get this from Resend -> Webhooks -> (your endpoint) -> Signing Secret
# after creating the endpoint. Required for the webhook to work at all -
# without it, every request to /api/webhooks/resend is rejected with 500.
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Prospect-email system (Growth CRM "Send Email" consultation invites) ---

# Absolute URL of Winsalot's own consultation-booking page
# (/book-consultation - see src/app/book-consultation/), used as the CTA
# link in every prospect consultation-invite email (opens in a new tab).
# Every send appends its own secure, single-purpose prefill token
# (?t=<token> - src/lib/winsalot-consultation-tokens.ts) so the public
# page can safely prefill that one prospect's info without exposing a raw
# database id. Set this to https://growth.winsalotcorp.com/book-consultation
# in production. If unset, malformed, or still pointing at the retired
# cleaning.winsalotcorp.com domain, getWinsalotBookingUrlBase()
# (src/lib/send-prospect-email.ts) falls back to that exact canonical URL
# instead of blocking sends - logged loudly (Vercel runtime logs) so the
# misconfiguration is still visible.
WINSALOT_BOOKING_URL=

# --- Winsalot consultation-booking system ---
# See docs/crm.md#consultation-booking for the full setup guide.

# Bearer secret for GET/POST /api/cron/winsalot-appointment-reminders (the
# automatic prospect-facing 24-hour + 1-hour consultation reminder job -
# see src/lib/winsalot-consultation-reminders.ts). This route is invoked
# by Supabase's pg_cron/pg_net (see
# supabase/migrations/0088_winsalot_consultations.sql), not by Vercel
# Cron, since Vercel Cron on this account's Hobby plan can only run once a
# day - far too coarse for a "1 hour before" reminder. Set the SAME value
# here (as a Vercel project env var) and in Supabase Vault as the
# 'winsalot_reminder_cron_secret' secret, and set
# 'winsalot_reminder_cron_url' in Vault to this deployment's
# https://<domain>/api/cron/winsalot-appointment-reminders - see that
# migration's header comment for the exact one-time setup steps.
# Deliberately a separate secret from every Lead Gen CRM reminder cron
# secret, and not gated by LEADGEN_REMINDER_CRON_ENABLED - this system is
# exclusively part of the Growth CRM.
WINSALOT_APPOINTMENT_REMINDER_CRON_SECRET=

# --- SMS appointment reminders (Twilio) ---
# See supabase/migrations/0125_appointment_sms_reminders.sql and
# src/lib/appointment-sms.ts for the full design. SMS reminders ride
# along inside the EXACT SAME cron jobs the email reminders above already
# use (runLeadgenAppointmentReminderJob, runLeadgenProspect1HourReminderJob,
# runWinsalotAppointmentReminderJob) - there is no separate SMS cron
# route, schedule, or secret to configure. Set every var in this section
# independently on BOTH Vercel projects (winsalot-funding and
# winsalot-leadgen-crm) - each project can use the same Twilio number/
# account or its own, this app does not assume either way.
#
# Get these three from the Twilio Console (https://console.twilio.com) ->
# Account -> API keys & tokens (Account SID / Auth Token) and Phone
# Numbers -> Manage -> Active Numbers (the SMS-capable number to send
# from, E.164 format, e.g. +14165551234).
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=

# Internal admin phone number (E.164, e.g. +14165551234) that receives an
# internal SMS notification 24 hours and 1 hour before EVERY appointment
# in both CRMs - never gated on prospect SMS consent (this is Winsalot's
# own internal notification, not a message to the prospect), and
# deduplicated the same way as every other reminder claim in this app -
# see the "admin" recipient_type rows in leadgen_appointment_sms_reminders
# / winsalot_appointment_sms_reminders. Leave unset to simply skip the
# admin notification (each attempt is recorded "Skipped" with a clear
# reason, never a hard failure).
ADMIN_NOTIFICATION_PHONE=

# Two Twilio webhooks to configure by hand, once per Vercel project/domain:
#
# 1. Delivery-status callback - NOTHING to configure in the Twilio
#    console for this one. It's set automatically, per-message, from
#    NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL (see smsStatusCallbackUrl() in src/lib/twilio.ts)
#    as https://<this deployment's domain>/api/webhooks/twilio/status -
#    just make sure NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL is correct on each project
#    (growth.winsalotcorp.com / leads.winsalotcorp.com in Production).
#    This is the ONLY thing allowed to move a reminder from "Sent" to
#    "Delivered"/"Failed" - the initial send only ever marks "Sent".
#
# 2. Inbound message webhook (STOP/START opt-out handling) - MUST be
#    configured by hand in the Twilio Console for each CRM's own
#    TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER: Phone Numbers -> Manage -> Active Numbers ->
#    (the number) -> Messaging Configuration -> "A MESSAGE COMES IN" ->
#    Webhook, HTTP POST, set to:
#      https://growth.winsalotcorp.com/api/webhooks/twilio/inbound   (Growth CRM's number)
#      https://leads.winsalotcorp.com/api/webhooks/twilio/inbound    (Lead Gen CRM's number)
#    Records STOP/START (and Twilio's standard synonyms - see
#    SMS_STOP_KEYWORDS/SMS_START_KEYWORDS in src/lib/appointment-sms.ts)
#    into the shared sms_opt_outs table, consulted before every
#    prospect-facing send in both CRMs. Both webhook routes verify
#    Twilio's X-Twilio-Signature header against this project's own
#    TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN above - requests that don't pass are rejected
#    with 403, so there is no separate webhook signing secret to set.
